### Insert Session Records

```ruby
put 'UserSession', 'S101', 'session:token', 'TOKEN101'
put 'UserSession', 'S101', 'session:status', 'Active'
put 'UserSession', 'S101', 'user:name', 'Yash'

put 'UserSession', 'S102', 'session:token', 'TOKEN102'
put 'UserSession', 'S102', 'session:status', 'Active'
put 'UserSession', 'S102', 'user:name', 'Rahul'
```

### Retrieve Session Data

```ruby
get 'UserSession', 'S101'
scan 'UserSession'
```

### Verify TTL

Wait for more than 60 seconds and then run:

```ruby
scan 'UserSession'
```

### Expected Output

Session column-family values expire after the configured TTL. Physical cleanup may happen later during HBase compaction, so expired data may not disappear immediately from storage.

